## Goal
Add an "ask" panel to the handler app (DEV-47). When a rule asks, the user picks the target for the link, with a "Remember" option that pins the choice as a new rule. The CLI and the decision log also need to cope with asking rules.

## Problems
None.

## Decision
- `routeLink` now calls `routeLinkAsk`, which takes the panel function (`handler.Ask`) and the remember function as parameters. Tests pass fakes. `routeLinkWith` passes nil for both, so it never asks and uses the default target.
- `routeAsked` opens the link first and only then writes the "Remember" rule. A failed write never delays or blocks the link. The failure goes into the log note.
- Remember writes through a locked `rulesfile.Remember`. If the rules file stopped asking while the panel was open, the write is skipped and the failure is noted.
- Cancelling (Esc) opens the default target. A link identical to one already waiting in a panel joins that panel and does not open twice.
- `decisionlog.AppendNote` adds an optional sixth log column, for example `asked -> Dia/Work, remembered "<name>"`. The note is cleaned to a single line and column. Without a note the log keeps five columns.
- The CLI cannot show a panel. `portero open` and `rules` print the cancel target and what Remember would pin. `--dry` lists a "would run" line per option. A real open and the web UI (`openUI`) use the default target and log `asked -> default (CLI)` (`openCLIAsked`).
- The native panel is in `internal/handler/panel.m`, with Go bindings in `ask.go` and a stub in `handler_other.go`.

